  "doc": "Body size classes and the tackle matrix (features/bodies/README.md). Bodies are circles of radius_m; on contact the overlap is split by mass (a body of mass m against M moves M/(m+M) of it). A contact whose closing speed is above tackle_mps is a run (a tackle), else a walk. rules: attacker class against defender class: walk and run results (shove = the mass split only; stagger = shoved knockback_m with no fall; knockdown = slides knockback_m, lies down_s, gets up and flees flee_s; blocked = the attacker stops at contact and the defender holds (the closing speed is removed, the tangent kept), the neutral rule for robots and bosses until the owner designs them). can_hurt: the contact may damage the defender (no tackle hurts anyone today).",
